  "content": {
    "id": "p32-q72-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "72",
    "prompt": "Complete the square of the following by adding the $2ab$ term.\n$$x^2+\\frac1{x^2}$$",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$\\left(x+\\dfrac1x\\right)^2-2$ or $\\left(x-\\dfrac1x\\right)^2+2$, where $x\\ne0$.",
      "worked": "For $x\\ne0$, the middle term is $2x\\left(\\frac1x\\right)=2$.\n$$\\begin{align*}x^2+\\frac1{x^2}&=x^2+2+\\frac1{x^2}-2\\\\x^2+\\frac1{x^2}&=\\left(x+\\frac1x\\right)^2-2.\\end{align*}$$\nAlternatively:\n$$\\begin{align*}x^2+\\frac1{x^2}&=x^2-2+\\frac1{x^2}+2\\\\x^2+\\frac1{x^2}&=\\left(x-\\frac1x\\right)^2+2.\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 20
  },
